  "content": {
    "id": "p14-p4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Determine whether the following statements are true or false.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-p4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p14-p4-a-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The difference of two even functions is neither even nor odd. ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "False",
                  "width": 20
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "Let $f$ and $g$ be even and define $h(x)=f(x)-g(x)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h(-x)&=f(-x)-g(-x)\\\\h(-x)&=f(x)-g(x)\\\\h(-x)&=h(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe difference is even, so the statement is false.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-p4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p14-p4-b-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The difference of two odd functions is odd. ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "True",
                  "width": 20
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "Let $f$ and $g$ be odd and define $h(x)=f(x)-g(x)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h(-x)&=f(-x)-g(-x)\\\\h(-x)&=-f(x)+g(x)\\\\h(-x)&=-\\bigl(f(x)-g(x)\\bigr)\\\\h(-x)&=-h(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe difference is odd, so the statement is true.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-p4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p14-p4-c-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The quotient of an even and odd function is even. ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "False",
                  "width": 20
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "Let $f$ be even and $g$ be odd, and define $h(x)=\\dfrac{f(x)}{g(x)}$ where $g(x)\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h(-x)&=\\frac{f(-x)}{g(-x)}\\\\h(-x)&=\\frac{f(x)}{-g(x)}\\\\h(-x)&=-h(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe quotient is odd where defined. It need not be even: for example, $f(x)=1$ and $g(x)=x$ give $h(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$, which is not even. Thus the statement is false.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      }
    ]
  },
